{
  "_comment": [
    "SDL-632: shared fixture for the public shell of a page. To be copied verbatim into",
    "pages-service/internal/shell/testdata/ (S4; no cross-service imports) — edit here, copy there.",
    "Each case: `doc`, `expect_shell`, optional `expect_cacheability`.",
    "`doc` is a page schema: v2 (rootId, nodes, parents, optional params), v1 ({ version: 1, root } — a nested tree), or a document carrying both root and nodes (both are cut). `expect_cacheability` is present only when `doc` has `nodes`.",
    "`expect_shell` is exactly what saunaPublicShell / shell.Strip must return for it — compare as JSON",
    "values (key order is irrelevant, array order is not).",
    "`expect_cacheability` maps node ids of `doc` to saunaNodeCacheability: full | guest-branch | none.",
    "Rules the cases pin: a node whose visibility is \"private\" — or any string that is not a mode, or",
    "a number/array — is removed with its subtree, reached through `children` AND `variants[].children`",
    "(and, for hand-written documents, through the `parents` chain); removed ids disappear from `nodes`,",
    "`parents`, every surviving `children[]` and `variants[].children`; `member` is removed from every",
    "node; `params` specs whose nodeId was removed are dropped, the key itself stays; a private root is",
    "reduced to { type }; nothing else changes.",
    "`guest_render_differs: true` marks a case where the shell deliberately draws differently for a guest",
    "A v1 `root` tree is cut by the same rules along `children`; a cut v1 root is reduced to { type }. `parents` is filtered when present and never invented when absent.",
    "`guest_render_differs: true` marks a case where the shell deliberately draws differently for a guest than the raw document does (fail closed); the engine's render-parity test skips it, Go may ignore it.",
    "`nodes` or `parents` present but not a plain object (an array, a string) — the shell drops BOTH keys, fail closed: no node reaches a visitor; the validator refuses such a document on write."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no private node: the shell is the document",
